import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout lang="en" title="About" altUrl="/about/">
  <p class="eyebrow">About this project</p>
  <h1>About this project</h1>
  <div class="body">
    <p class="lead">
      <em>Self Observatory</em> is a personal knowledge garden — not a chronological blog, but a place where
      notes grow and connect. The underlying idea is <strong>a life in relationship</strong>: with the world
      outside, and with oneself.
    </p>

    <h2>Two kinds of notes</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Field Notes</strong> record my encounters with the outside world — people, communities, the city,
      events, things I observe. <strong>Insight Notes</strong> turn inward — reflections, beliefs, questions, and
      how I slowly come to understand and change.
    </p>

    <h2>How to read</h2>
    <p>
      You can read linearly through each section, or wander by <strong>topic</strong> (broad regions of thought)
      and <strong>hashtag</strong> (specific labels) on the <a href="/en/explore/">Explore</a> page. The
      <a href="/en/map/">Constellation Map</a> draws the notes as stars: the lines show where the two directions
      of observation meet — through a shared topic, a shared hashtag, or a connection I set deliberately.
    </p>

    <h2>Writing principles</h2>
    <p>
      Slow and deliberate. Each note carries only a few hashtags, and links only to notes that are truly related —
      so the map stays meaningful instead of turning into a spiderweb. The site is intentionally light: text first,
      images heavily compressed, video embedded from elsewhere.
    </p>

    <h2>Bilingual</h2>
    <p>
      Vietnamese is the primary language. Every note has an English counterpart; use the VI / EN switch at the top
      to move between them. Want to discuss? Each note has buttons to share to social media — that's where the
      conversations happen.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
